{"id":"mahabharata-5-103","work":"mahabharata","part":5,"partName":"उद्योगपर्व","partNameEn":"Udyoga Parva","unit":103,"title":"त्र्यधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 103 · Garuda's pride humbled","summary":{"en":"Garuda, enraged at losing his prey, goes to Indra and boasts that he carries Vishnu himself and is the mightiest of all. Vishnu lays one arm on him, and Garuda, crushed by its weight, falls senseless and begs forgiveness; Kanva warns Duryodhana that he too will be humbled if he does not make peace.","kn":"ತನ್ನ ಬೇಟೆ ತಪ್ಪಿದ್ದಕ್ಕೆ ಕೋಪಗೊಂಡ ಗರುಡನು ಇಂದ್ರನ ಬಳಿ ಹೋಗಿ ವಿಷ್ಣುವನ್ನೇ ಹೊರುವ ತಾನೇ ಎಲ್ಲರಿಗಿಂತ ಬಲಿಷ್ಠನೆಂದು ಬಡಾಯಿ ಕೊಚ್ಚುತ್ತಾನೆ. ವಿಷ್ಣು ತನ್ನ ಒಂದು ತೋಳನ್ನು ಅವನ ಮೇಲಿಡುತ್ತಾನೆ, ಅದರ ಭಾರಕ್ಕೆ ಕುಸಿದ ಗರುಡನು ಪ್ರಜ್ಞೆತಪ್ಪಿ ಕ್ಷಮೆ ಬೇಡುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಸಂಧಿ ಮಾಡದಿದ್ದರೆ ನೀನೂ ಹೀಗೆಯೇ ವಿನಯಗೊಳ್ಳುವೆ ಎಂದು ಕಣ್ವರು ದುರ್ಯೋಧನನನ್ನು ಎಚ್ಚರಿಸುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"शिकार छिन जाने से क्रुद्ध गरुड़ इन्द्र के पास जाकर डींग मारता है कि वह स्वयं विष्णु को ढोता है और सबसे बलवान है। विष्णु अपनी एक भुजा उस पर रखते हैं, और उसके भार से कुचला गरुड़ मूर्च्छित होकर क्षमा माँगता है; कण्व दुर्योधन को चेताते हैं कि यदि वह सन्धि नहीं करेगा तो वह भी ऐसे ही विनम्र किया जाएगा।","te":"వేట తప్పిపోయినందుకు కోపించిన గరుడుడు ఇంద్రుని దగ్గరకు వెళ్లి విష్ణువునే మోసే తానే అందరికంటే బలవంతుడినని గొప్పలు చెబుతాడు. విష్ణువు తన ఒక భుజాన్ని అతనిపై ఉంచగా దాని బరువుకు నలిగిన గరుడుడు స్పృహ తప్పి క్షమించమని వేడుకుంటాడు; సంధి చేయకపోతే నీవూ ఇలాగే వినయం పొందుతావని కణ్వుడు దుర్యోధనుని హెచ్చరిస్తాడు.","ta":"தன் இரை பறிபோனதால் சினமுற்ற கருடன் இந்திரனிடம் சென்று விஷ்ணுவையே சுமப்பவன் நானே எல்லாரிலும் வலியவன் என்று வீம்பு பேசுகிறான். விஷ்ணு தம் ஒரு கையை அவன் மேல் வைக்க, அதன் பாரத்தால் நசுங்கிய கருடன் மயங்கி மன்னிப்பு வேண்டுகிறான்; சமாதானம் செய்யாவிட்டால் நீயும் இவ்வாறே பணியவைக்கப்படுவாய் என்று கண்வர் துரியோதனனை எச்சரிக்கிறார்.","ml":"ഇര നഷ്ടപ്പെട്ടതിൽ കോപിച്ച ഗരുഡൻ ഇന്ദ്രന്റെ അടുത്തെത്തി, വിഷ്ണുവിനെ താൻ തന്നെ വഹിക്കുന്നുവെന്നും താനാണ് ഏറ്റവും ശക്തനെന്നും വീമ്പിളക്കുന്നു. വിഷ്ണു ഒരു കൈ അദ്ദേഹത്തിന്റെ മേൽ വെക്കുന്നു; ആ ഭാരത്തിൽ ഞെരുങ്ങി ഗരുഡൻ ബോധരഹിതനായി വീണ്, മാപ്പ് യാചിക്കുന്നു. സന്ധി ചെയ്യാത്തപക്ഷം ദുര്യോധനനും താഴ്ത്തപ്പെടുമെന്ന് കണ്വൻ മുന്നറിയിപ്പ് നൽകുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 5.103; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jan 23 2024","sections":[{"title":"भगवद्यानपर्व","titleEn":"Bhagavadyana Parva (Krishna's embassy)","verses":[{"text":"कण्व उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Kanva said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"गरुडस्तत्तु शुश्राव यथावृत्तं महाबलः ।\nआयुःप्रदानं शक्रेण कृतं नागस्य भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"The mighty Garuda heard exactly what had happened: that Indra had granted the serpent a life span, Bharata."}},{"n":2,"text":"पक्षवातेन महता रुद्ध्वा त्रिभुवनं खगः ।\nसुपर्णः परमक्रुद्धो वासवं समुपाद्रवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Filling the three worlds with the great wind of his wings, the bird Suparna rushed at Indra in great fury."}},{"text":"गरुड उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Garuda said:"}},{"n":3,"text":"भगवन्किमवज्ञानात्क्षुधां प्रति भये मम ।\nकामकारवरं दत्त्वा पुनश्चलितवानसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"'Lord, why, out of contempt, do you now turn back and frustrate me, who am afraid of hunger, after granting me the boon of eating as I please?"}},{"n":4,"text":"निसर्गात्सर्वभूतानां सर्वभूतेश्वरेण मे ।\nआहारो विहितो धात्रा किमर्थं वार्यते त्वया ॥","meaning":{"en":"The creator, lord of all beings, ordained food for me by nature, as for all creatures. Why do you forbid it?"}},{"n":5,"text":"वृतश्चैष महानागः स्थापितः समयश्च मे ।\nअनेन च मया देव भर्तव्यः प्रसवो महान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great serpent was chosen, and an agreement was made. With him I must support my many offspring."}},{"n":6,"text":"एतस्मिंस्त्वन्यथाभूते नान्यं हिंसितुमुत्सहे ।\nक्रीडसे कामकारेण देवराज यथेच्छकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Since this has turned out otherwise, I cannot bring myself to harm another. King of the gods, you play as you please, at will."}},{"n":7,"text":"सोऽहं प्राणान्विमोक्ष्यामि तथा परिजनो मम ।\nये च भृत्या मम गृहे प्रीतिमान्भव वासव ॥","meaning":{"en":"So I shall give up my life, and so will my household and the servants in my home. Be pleased, Indra."}},{"n":8,"text":"एतच्चैवाहमर्हामि भूयश्च बलवृत्रहन् ।\nत्रैलोक्यस्येश्वरो योऽहं परभृत्यत्वमागतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"This I deserve, and more, slayer of Bala and Vritra, I who am lord of the three worlds yet have come to serve another."}},{"n":9,"text":"त्वयि तिष्ठति देवेश न विष्णुः कारणं मम ।\nत्रैलोक्यराज राज्यं हि त्वयि वासव शाश्वतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"While you stand, lord of the gods, Vishnu is not my reason. King of the three worlds, sovereignty rests eternally with you, Indra."}},{"n":10,"text":"ममापि दक्षस्य सुता जननी कश्यपः पिता ।\nअहमप्युत्सहे लोकान्समस्तान्वोढुमञ्जसा ॥","meaning":{"en":"My mother too is a daughter of Daksha, and Kashyapa is my father. I too can easily carry all the worlds."}},{"n":11,"text":"असह्यं सर्वभूतानां ममापि विपुलं बलम् ।\nमयापि सुमहत्कर्म कृतं दैतेयविग्रहे ॥","meaning":{"en":"My great strength too is unbearable to all beings. I too did a mighty deed in the war with the Daityas."}},{"n":12,"text":"श्रुतश्रीः श्रुतसेनश्च विवस्वान्रोचनामुखः ।\nप्रसभः कालकाक्षश्च मयापि दितिजा हताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shrutashri, Shrutasena, Vivasvan, Rochanamukha, Prasabha and Kalakaksha, these sons of Diti were killed by me too."}},{"n":13,"text":"यत्तु ध्वजस्थानगतो यत्नात्परिचराम्यहम् ।\nवहामि चैवानुजं ते तेन मामवमन्यसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Because I carefully serve and carry your younger brother, abiding on his banner, you hold me in contempt."}},{"n":14,"text":"कोऽन्यो भारसहो ह्यस्ति कोऽन्योऽस्ति बलवत्तरः ।\nमया योऽहं विशिष्टः सन्वहामीमं सबान्धवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Who else can bear such a load? Who else is stronger? I, being greater than others, carry him with his kinsmen."}},{"n":15,"text":"अवज्ञाय तु यत्तेऽहं भोजनाद्व्यपरोपितः ।\nतेन मे गौरवं नष्टं त्वत्तश्चास्माच्च वासव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Because you disregarded me and cut me off from my food, I have lost my respect for you, Indra, and for him."}},{"n":16,"text":"अदित्यां य इमे जाता बलविक्रमशालिनः ।\nत्वमेषां किल सर्वेषां विशेषाद्बलवत्तरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"These sons born of Aditi are rich in strength and valor, and you are, they say, the strongest of all."}},{"n":17,"text":"सोऽहं पक्षैकदेशेन वहामि त्वां गतक्लमः ।\nविमृश त्वं शनैस्तात को न्वत्र बलवानिति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yet with just a part of one wing I carry you without fatigue. Think about it calmly, dear one: who is really the stronger here?'"}},{"text":"कण्व उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Kanva said:"}},{"n":18,"text":"तस्य तद्वचनं श्रुत्वा खगस्योदर्कदारुणम् ।\nअक्षोभ्यं क्षोभयंस्तार्क्ष्यमुवाच रथचक्रभृत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing the bird's words, which were harsh in their outcome, the bearer of the discus chariot-wheel spoke to Garuda, unshakable though he was, to unsettle him."}},{"n":19,"text":"गरुत्मन्मन्यसेऽऽत्मानं बलवन्तं सुदुर्बलम् ।\nअलमस्मत्समक्षं ते स्तोतुमात्मानमण्डज ॥","meaning":{"en":"'Garutman, you think yourself strong, but you are very weak. Enough, egg-born one, of praising yourself in front of me."}},{"n":20,"text":"त्रैलोक्यमपि मे कृत्स्नमशक्तं देहधारणे ।\nअहमेवात्मनात्मानं वहामि त्वां च धारये ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even the whole of the three worlds is not able to support my body. I carry myself by myself, and I carry you too."}},{"n":21,"text":"इमं तावन्ममैकं त्वं बाहुं सव्येतरं वह ।\nयद्येनं धारयस्येकं सफलं ते विकत्थितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"For now, bear just this one arm of mine, the left one. If you can support even this one, your boast will be proved true.'"}},{"n":22,"text":"ततः स भगवांस्तस्य स्कन्धे बाहुं समासजत् ।\nनिपपात स भारार्तो विह्वलो नष्टचेतनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the Lord laid his arm on Garuda's shoulder. Garuda collapsed, tormented by the load, bewildered and losing his senses."}},{"n":23,"text":"यावान्हि भारः कृत्स्नायाः पृथिव्याः पर्वतैः सह ।\nएकस्या देहशाखायास्तावद्भारममन्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"The weight of the whole earth with its mountains seemed to him no more than the weight of one branch of that body."}},{"n":24,"text":"न त्वेनं पीडयामास बलेन बलवत्तरः ।\nततो हि जीवितं तस्य न व्यनीनशदच्युतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yet Vishnu, the stronger, did not crush him with force, and so the bird's life did not perish, for Achyuta spared him."}},{"n":25,"text":"विपक्षः स्रस्तकायश्च विचेता विह्वलः खगः ।\nमुमोच पत्राणि तदा गुरुभारप्रपीडितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wingless, his body sagging, senseless and stunned, the bird, crushed by the heavy weight, let his feathers fall."}},{"n":26,"text":"स विष्णुं शिरसा पक्षी प्रणम्य विनतासुतः ।\nविचेता विह्वलो दीनः किंचिद्वचनमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Vinata's son bowed his head to Vishnu and, senseless, stunned and wretched, said a few words."}},{"n":27,"text":"भगवँल्लोकसारस्य सदृशेन वपुष्मता ।\nभुजेन स्वैरमुक्तेन निष्पिष्टोऽस्मि महीतले ॥","meaning":{"en":"'Lord, I have been crushed on the ground by an arm worthy of the essence of the worlds, which you let fall at ease."}},{"n":28,"text":"क्षन्तुमर्हसि मे देव विह्वलस्याल्पचेतसः ।\nबलदाहविदग्धस्य पक्षिणो ध्वजवासिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Forgive me, God, I who was bewildered and foolish, a bird living on your banner, burnt up by the fire of pride in strength."}},{"n":29,"text":"न विज्ञातं बलं देव मया ते परमं विभो ।\nतेन मन्याम्यहं वीर्यमात्मनोऽसदृशं परैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I did not know your supreme strength, Lord, and so I thought my own might was unequaled by others.'"}},{"n":30,"text":"ततश्चक्रे स भगवान्प्रसादं वै गरुत्मतः ।\nमैवं भूय इति स्नेहात्तदा चैनमुवाच ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the Lord showed favor to Garuda and said to him out of affection, 'Never again act so.'"}},{"n":31,"text":"तथा त्वमपि गान्धारे यावत्पाण्डुसुतान्रणे ।\nनासादयसि तान्वीरांस्तावज्जीवसि पुत्रक ॥","meaning":{"en":"'So too you, son of Gandhari, live only as long as you do not meet those heroes, the sons of Pandu, in battle, my child."}},{"n":32,"text":"भीमः प्रहरतां श्रेष्ठो वायुपुत्रो महाबलः ।\nधनंजयश्चेन्द्रसुतो न हन्यातां तु कं रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhima, best of fighters, the mighty son of the wind, and Dhananjaya, Indra's son, whom would they not kill in battle?"}},{"n":33,"text":"विष्णुर्वायुश्च शक्रश्च धर्मस्तौ चाश्विनावुभौ ।\nएते देवास्त्वया केन हेतुना शक्यमीक्षितुम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vishnu, Vayu, Indra, Dharma and the two Ashvins are the gods behind them. For what reason could you hope to face these gods?"}},{"n":34,"text":"तदलं ते विरोधेन शमं गच्छ नृपात्मज ।\nवासुदेवेन तीर्थेन कुलं रक्षितुमर्हसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Enough of your hostility. Make peace, prince. Through Vasudeva as the sacred ford you can protect your family."}},{"n":35,"text":"प्रत्यक्षो ह्यस्य सर्वस्य नारदोऽयं महातपाः ।\nमाहात्म्यं यत्तदा विष्णोर्योऽयं चक्रगदाधरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"This Narada of great austerity is a direct witness to all this, and to the greatness of Vishnu, who is this bearer of discus and mace.'"}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":36,"text":"दुर्योधनस्तु तच्छ्रुत्वा निःश्वसन्भृकुटीमुखः ।\nराधेयमभिसंप्रेक्ष्य जहास स्वनवत्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"But Duryodhana, hearing this, sighed with a frowning face, looked at Radheya Karna and laughed aloud."}},{"n":37,"text":"कदर्थीकृत्य तद्वाक्यमृषेः कण्वस्य दुर्मतिः ।\nऊरुं गजकराकारं ताडयन्निदमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The wicked-minded prince made light of the sage Kanva's words, and slapping his thigh, which was shaped like an elephant's trunk, said this."}},{"n":38,"text":"यथैवेश्वरसृष्टोऽस्मि यद्भावि या च मे गतिः ।\nतथा महर्षे वर्तामि किं प्रलापः करिष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"'As the Lord has made me, and whatever my future and fate will be, so I shall act, great sage. What will idle talk achieve?'"}}]}]}